The context explicitly mentions hand-crafted features such as lexical and syntactic features.

Prior approaches use hand-crafted features, e.g., lexical and syntactic features, fed into a linear classifier with a fixed threshold [3]. These features heavily rely on system or human annotations [4][5], and are mostly about syntactic-head or topic information [5].
